  "traits": {
    "covering": {
      "value": "skin",
      "note": "Its thick, wrinkled gray skin has only scattered hairs.",
      "source": "adw"
    },
    "size": {
      "value": "huge",
      "note": "Females weigh 2,000 to 3,500 kg and males 4,500 to 6,100 kg.",
      "source": "adw"
    },
    "diet": {
      "value": "plants",
      "note": "It eats grass, leaves, fruit, roots and bark.",
      "source": "adw"
    },
    "activity": {
      "value": "any",
      "note": "It feeds for most of the day and night and sleeps only about 4 hours.",
      "source": "adw"
    },
    "social": {
      "value": "groups",
      "note": "Herds of mothers and young follow the oldest female; adult males often live alone.",
      "source": "adw"
    },
    "trees": {
      "value": "no",
      "note": "It walks on the ground and never climbs.",
      "source": "adw"
    },
    "birth": {
      "value": "live",
      "source": "adw"
    },
    "young": {
      "value": "one",
      "note": "A mother has one calf, rarely twins, every 3 to 9 years.",
      "source": "adw"
    },
    "lifespan": {
      "value": "long",
      "note": "It can live 60 to 70 years.",
      "source": "adw"
    }
  },
  "clues": [
    {
      "category": "morphology",
      "text": "Both males and females have big, curved ivory tusks.",
      "tags": [
        "tusks"
      ],
      "source": "adw"
    },
    {
      "category": "morphology",
      "text": "Its huge ears help it cool down on hot days.",
      "source": "adw"
    },
    {
      "category": "morphology",
      "text": "The tip of its trunk has two finger-like points for picking things up.",
      "tags": [
        "trunk"
      ],
      "source": "wikipedia"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "It sprays mud and water over itself with its trunk to keep its skin cool and healthy.",
      "source": "adw"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "It talks with deep rumbles that other elephants can hear more than 2 km away.",
      "source": "adw"
    },
    {
      "category": "diet",
      "text": "It pushes over whole trees to reach their roots and bark.",
      "source": "adw"
    },
    {
      "category": "habitat",
      "text": "It lives from mountain forests and swamps to dry deserts, and walks long distances to find water and food.",
      "source": "iucn"
    },
    {
      "category": "conservation",
      "text": "Farms and towns taking its land, and poaching for ivory, are its main threats.",
      "source": "wikipedia"
    },
    {
      "category": "morphology",
      "text": "Some of its teeth keep growing all its life.",
      "tags": [
        "ever_growing_teeth"
      ],
      "source": "sdzwa",
      "url": "https://ielc.libguides.com/sdzg/factsheets/african_elephant/characteristics"
    },
    {
      "category": "morphology",
      "text": "It has very sharp hearing and relies on it.",
      "tags": [
        "super_hearing"
      ],
      "source": "adw"
    },
    {
      "category": "morphology",
      "text": "Its ears are large for its head.",
      "tags": [
        "big_ears"
      ],
      "source": "adw"
    },
    {
      "category": "diet",
      "text": "Leaves are a main part of its food.",
      "tags": [
        "leaf_eater"
      ],
      "source": "adw"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "It makes loud calls that carry far, such as songs, hoots, barks, roars or wails.",
      "tags": [
        "loud_calls"
      ],
      "source": "adw"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "It never climbs trees: it stays on or under the ground, or in water.",
      "tags": [
        "never_climbs"
      ],
      "source": "adw"
    },
    {
      "category": "diet",
      "text": "It visits salt licks, or eats mineral-rich soil, clay or water, to get minerals.",
      "tags": [
        "salt_licks"
      ],
      "source": "wikipedia"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "It marks its home area, paths or objects with scent, such as urine, dung or scent rubbed on from its glands.",
      "tags": [
        "scent_marks"
      ],
      "source": "adw"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "It makes loud, harsh screeches.",
      "tags": [
        "screecher"
      ],
      "source": "sdzwa",
      "url": "https://ielc.libguides.com/sdzg/factsheets/african_elephant/behavior"
    },
    {
      "category": "diet",
      "text": "It spreads plant seeds to new places by eating them, often in fruit, and passing them in its droppings.",
      "tags": [
        "seed_spreader"
      ],
      "source": "wikipedia"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "It can feel vibrations or ripples through the ground or water, to sense prey, danger or others.",
      "tags": [
        "senses_vibrations"
      ],
      "source": "government",
      "url": "https://www.sanbi.org/animal-of-the-week/african-elephant/"
    },
    {
      "category": "morphology",
      "text": "It can breathe through the tip of its raised nose, snout or trunk while the rest of its body stays under water.",
      "tags": [
        "snorkel_nose"
      ],
      "source": "sdzwa",
      "url": "https://blogs.sandiegozoo.org/story-hub/2026/understanding-elephant-behavior-interactions"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "At least sometimes, it stands, rears up, hops or runs on its back legs alone.",
      "tags": [
        "stands_on_hind_legs"
      ],
      "source": "government",
      "url": "https://www.sanbi.org/animal-of-the-week/african-elephant/"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "It swims well or often.",
      "tags": [
        "swimmer"
      ],
      "source": "sdzwa",
      "url": "https://blogs.sandiegozoo.org/story-hub/2026/03/02/welcome-denny-sanford-elephant-valley"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "It uses objects such as sticks or stones as tools to get food or do tasks.",
      "tags": [
        "uses_tools"
      ],
      "source": "government",
      "url": "https://www.sanbi.org/animal-of-the-week/african-elephant/"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "It calls with deep, low rumbles, some too low for people to hear.",
      "tags": [
        "low_rumbles"
      ],
      "source": "adw"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "It wallows in mud, or coats itself with mud, to cool off or protect its skin.",
      "tags": [
        "mud_bather"
      ],
      "source": "adw"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "It has no fixed home area: it wanders or travels long distances, following food, water or rain.",
      "tags": [
        "nomadic"
      ],
      "source": "iucn"
    },
    {
      "category": "diet",
      "text": "It pushes or knocks over whole trees to feed.",
      "tags": [
        "pushes_over_trees"
      ],
      "source": "adw"
    },
    {
      "category": "habitat",
      "text": "It lives at least partly in forest with a thick undergrowth of bamboo.",
      "tags": [
        "bamboo_forest"
      ],
      "source": "ngo",
      "url": "https://www.savetheelephants.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/2008StatusofKenyasElephants.pdf"
    },
    {
      "category": "habitat",
      "text": "It lives at least partly high up in mountains: on upper slopes, high plateaus or alpine zones, not just foothills.",
      "tags": [
        "high_mountains"
      ],
      "source": "ngo",
      "url": "https://www.savetheelephants.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/2008StatusofKenyasElephants.pdf"
    },
    {
      "category": "habitat",
      "text": "It lives at least partly in dry, thorny forest or brush.",
      "tags": [
        "spiny_forest"
      ],
      "source": "sdzwa",
      "url": "https://ielc.libguides.com/sdzg/factsheets/african_elephant/distribution"
    }
  ],
  "facts": [
    {
      "category": "key_fact",
      "text": "It is the largest land animal alive today.",
      "source": "adw"
    },
    {
      "category": "key_fact",
      "text": "A mother is pregnant for about 22 months, longer than any other mammal.",
      "source": "wikipedia"
    },
    {
      "category": "key_fact",
      "text": "In Gorongosa, Mozambique, so many tusked elephants were poached during a war that more tuskless females were born afterward.",
      "source": "literature",
      "url": "https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abe7389"
    },
    {
      "category": "behavior",
      "text": "By knocking down trees, it keeps grassland open and makes homes for frogs and lizards.",
      "source": "adw"
    },
    {
      "category": "diet_flora",
      "text": "An adult eats about 150 kg of plants and drinks about 230 L of water a day.",
      "source": "wikipedia"
    },
    {
      "category": "life_description",
      "text": "A newborn calf weighs about 100 kg and stays close to its mother until about 8 years old.",
      "source": "adw"
    },
    {
      "category": "threat",
      "text": "Since 2021 the Red List has judged it apart from the forest elephant, and listed it as Endangered.",
      "source": "wikipedia"
    }
  ],
